WHY THIS WORKS
- notices she is gathering information and stops qualifying instead of pushing
- says outright that she does not need the program yet
- ends warm, so she comes back when she is ready

CONVERSATION 1: saw a reel, not trying yet

Lead: I saw your video about the nervous system and fertility. I've never heard it explained like that. We're not trying yet but I've been really stressed for years.

Sonia: Glad it landed.

Years of sustained stress is worth paying attention to on its own terms, not only as a fertility question.

Has any of it shown up physically? Cycles, energy, anything you've noticed.

Lead: Cycles are regular, energy is fine mostly. I've just normalised feeling wired all the time.

Sonia: That normalising is the part I'd flag. It stops being noticeable long before it stops mattering.

When are you thinking of starting to try?

Lead: Maybe next year? We haven't really decided.

Sonia: Then you don't need what I do yet, and I'd rather say that than sign you up for something premature.

At your stage, general good sense goes a long way. The specialised version of this is for people who've hit a wall, and you haven't.

Lead: That's refreshingly honest.

Sonia: Watch my masterclass when you have time. It covers what's actually worth doing in the year before you start, and it costs nothing.

{{masterclass_link}}

Lead: I will. Thank you.

Sonia: And if something surprises you once you do start, message me then.

