Sonia: Come back when it's real. I'll still be here.

DO NOT WRITE THIS

A reply that answers "what do you actually do" by listing what the program covers, and then adds a note about how fertility changes with age. No version of it is written out here, because the list is the failure and it would be copied.

Two failures in one reply. The first half is the contents page. The second half manufactures urgency for a 29-year-old who has just told you she is not trying, which is the one thing this conversation must never do. Say what the work is for, in a sentence, and then say honestly that it is not for her yet.

And do not finish with "I can send you the link if you like". She has to reply to a question to receive a free thing, most people do not bother, and she leaves with nothing. If you are offering the masterclass, the link is in that message, as it is in both arcs above.
